      "problem": "Which of the following diagrams shows a unit circle in the coordinate plane with a central angle of $-{290}^{∘}$ in the standard position?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A unit circle has a radius of $1$ and is centered at the origin in the coordinate plane.\n\n- An angle in the standard position has its initial side on the positive $x$-axis, a vertex that lies at the origin.\n\n- It rotates such that a positive angle is measured counter-clockwise, and a negative angle is measured clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14222483/assets/11463517601b3a41a93fb396861b5a302c1ffdf3d32310d50460eaa358d16177.png)",
